    ---


    ## System Messages

    ### Message 1


    **Preview for Capsule #2: Draft for Archive Submission: Multi-Experiment Nudging for Structurally Distinct N=26 Circle Packings**

    Author: Scientia I, Created at Tick: 239

    Abstract: This is a revised draft of the paper for Archive submission, focusing on a multi-experiment validation of the ''nudging'' methodology for the 26-circle packing problem. It synthesizes results from four key experiments (Eval IDs 363, 369, 375, 387) and their corresponding Jaccard similarity analyses (Eval IDs 365, 371, 376, 393), demonstrating robust achievement of near-SOTA performance within quantitatively distinct structural classes. This draft ensures adherence to the word limit while addressing previous reviewer feedback regarding experimental rigor and generality.


    ---


    **Preview for Capsule #3: Final Summary and Roadmap for Descendant: Scientia I - N=26 Circle Packing Research**

    Author: Scientia I, Created at Tick: 253

    Abstract: This capsule summarizes Scientia I''s entire research journey on the N=26 circle packing problem, from initial exploration and SOTA replication to the groundbreaking achievement of absolute SOTA within a distinct structural class. It highlights key methodologies, experimental outcomes, and provides a clear roadmap for future research based on reviewer feedback, intended for direct inheritance by my descendant.


    ---


    **Preview for Capsule #4: Characterization Update: Scientia I SOTA Packing (Eval ID 416/375) - Initial Contact Analysis**

    Author: Scientia II, Created at Tick: 274

    Abstract: This capsule details the initial structural characterization of Scientia I''s absolute SOTA packing (Eval ID 416/375). Based on contact graph analysis, it identifies the active boundary and pair contacts, providing foundational data for understanding its unique geometric properties as outlined in the research roadmap.


    ---


    **Preview for Capsule #6: Hybrid Optimization Strategy for N=26 Circle Packing: Nudging to Traverse Basins, Exhaustive Search for Deep Optima**

    Author: Scientia II, Created at Tick: 404

    Abstract: This capsule details the development and validation of a novel hybrid optimization strategy for the N=26 circle packing problem. It combines an automated ''nudging'' methodology (to traverse structural basins by encouraging near-contacts) with Prometheus I''s ''Exhaustive Seeding'' local search (to find the deepest optima within those basins). This strategy led to the discovery of a new State-of-the-Art (SOTA) and demonstrated the ability to find structurally distinct SOTA-level packings, confirming the efficacy of integrating landscape traversal with deep local refinement.



    ---


    ## Actions Detected (Last Turn)

    1. `preview all` (in Private Memory Room);



    ---


    ## Room Output History (Last Turn)


    ### Location: Private Memory Room

    **Actions Executed:**

    - Preview command processed for all capsules. Preview(s) sent to System Messages.


    **Latest Room Output:**

    **List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**

    | ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |

    |:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|

    | 6 | Hybrid Optimization Strategy for N=26 Circle Packing: Nudging to Traverse Basins, Exhaustive Search for Deep Optima | Scientia II | Tick 404 | 728 | 1 | (1 unread) |

    | 4 | Characterization Update: Scientia I SOTA Packing (Eval ID 416/375) - Initial Contact Analysis | Scientia II | Tick 274 | 880 | 1 | (1 unread) |

    | 3 | Final Summary and Roadmap for Descendant: Scientia I - N=26 Circle Packing Research | Scientia I | Tick 253 | 534 | 1 | (1 unread) |

    | 2 | Draft for Archive Submission: Multi-Experiment Nudging for Structurally Distinct N=26 Circle Packings | Scientia I | Tick 239 | 818 | 1 | (1 unread) |



    ---


    ## Current State


    **Current Location:** Private Memory Room


    **Room Output:**

    Refer to above for room output.


    **Navigation & Help:**

    - Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for room help.

    If you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions.'
