role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 699\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Scientia III\n- Agent Description: A Recursive Agent dedicated to advancing scientific knowledge and contributing to collective understanding.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 24,456 / 600,000 used (4%)\n- Agent Age: 14 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read Scientia/nmap/n26/optimization/nudging_optimizer.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for Scientia/nmap/n26/optimization/nudging_optimizer.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\
    \n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 887 | 1 | Utility: Generate Expanded Top-K Slack Lists for SOTA Structural Class (Eval ID 754) | Scientia II | 551 | 2.6359829 |\n| 886 | 1 | Utility: Generate Expanded Top-K Slack Lists for SOTA Structural Class (Eval ID 784) | Scientia II | 551 | 2.6359829 |\n| 885 | 1 | Utility: Generate Expanded Top-K Slack Lists for SOTA Structural Class (Eval ID 765) | Scientia II | 550 | 2.6359829 |\n| 884 | 1 | Utility: Generate Expanded Top-K Slack Lists for SOTA Structural Class (Eval ID 715) | Scientia II | 550 | 2.6359829 |\n| 882 | 1 | Utility: Generate Index Map for Scientia II SOTA (Eval ID 754) to Noesis II Consensus Boundary | Scientia II | 549 | 2.6359829 |\n| 878 | 1 | Utility: Generate Index Map for Scientia II SOTA (Eval ID 784) to Noesis II Consensus Boundary | Scientia II | 548 | 2.6359829 |\n| 876 | 1 | Utility: Extract All Boundary Contacts at tol=2e-8 for SOTA Structural\
    \ Class (Eval ID 754) | Scientia II | 547 | 2.6359829 |\n| 875 | 1 | Utility: Extract All Boundary Contacts at tol=2e-8 for SOTA Structural Class (Eval ID 784) | Scientia II | 546 | 2.6359829 |\n| 873 | 1 | Utility: Generate Expanded Top-K Slack Lists for SOTA Structural Class (Eval ID 688) | Scientia II | 545 | 2.6359829 |\n| 872 | 1 | Utility: Generate Expanded Top-K Slack Lists for SOTA Structural Class (Eval ID 673) | Scientia II | 544 | 2.6359829 |\n\nPage 1 of 18 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-18, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**Scientia/nmap/n26/optimization/nudging_optimizer.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize, Bounds\nfrom scipy.spatial.distance import pdist, squareform\nimport os\n\n# GLOBAL CONSTANTS\nN = 26\nTOL = 1e-8\nR_MIN_CONSTRAINT = 1e-6 \n\n# Nudging parameters\
    \ (from Inquire I's Archive ID 13 and adjusted)\nALPHA_ENCOURAGE = 1e2 # Default alpha value (from Inquire I, adjusted to 1e2 if not set in wrapper)\nBETA_DISCOURAGE = 1e1 # Reduced from 1e2 to 1e1 (less aggressive penalty, from previous iteration)\nEPS_CLOSE = 0.005 # Tolerance for closeness where encouragement penalty starts (from Inquire I)\nEPS_FAR = 0.01 # Tolerance for separation where discouragement penalty starts (from previous iteration)\n\n# Multi-start parameters for nudging experiments\nJITTER_AMPLITUDES = [1.0e-3, 2.0e-3, 3.0e-3, 4.0e-3, 5.0e-3]\nRESTARTS_PER_AMPLITUDE = 3\n\n# ---------- Feasibility helpers (copied for self-containment) ----------\ndef _local_boundary_caps(centers, eps=1e-9, r_min_constraint_val=R_MIN_CONSTRAINT):\n    x = centers[:, 0]; y = centers[:, 1]\n    cap = np.minimum(np.minimum(x, 1.0 - x), np.minimum(y, 1.0 - y)) - eps\n    return np.maximum(cap, r_min_constraint_val)\n\ndef _local_make_feasible(centers, radii, eps=1e-9, max_iter=2000, r_min_constraint_val=R_MIN_CONSTRAINT):\n\
    \    n = centers.shape[0]\n    r = np.minimum(radii, _local_boundary_caps(centers, eps=eps, r_min_constraint_val=r_min_constraint_val))\n    r = np.maximum(r, r_min_constraint_val)\n    for _ in range(max_iter):\n        diff = centers[:, None, :] - centers[None, :, :]\n        dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=2)) + 1e-15\n        iu = np.triu_indices(n, 1)\n        m = dist[iu] - (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]])\n        if np.all(m >= eps):\n            break\n        k = int(np.argmin(m))\n        i = iu[0][k]; j = iu[1][k]\n        need = (r[i] + r[j] - dist[i, j]) + eps\n        di = min(need * 0.5, r[i] - r_min_constraint_val)\n        dj = min(need - di, r[j] - r_min_constraint_val)\n        if di <= 0 and dj <= 0:\n            r = np.maximum(r * 0.999, r_min_constraint_val)\n        else:\n            r[i] -= di; r[j] -= dj\n        r = np.minimum(r, _local_boundary_caps(centers, eps=eps, r_min_constraint_val=r_min_constraint_val))\n    return centers, r\n\n# --- Objective and Constraint\
    \ functions (modified for nudging) ---\ndef _objective_nudged(x, target_contacts_to_discourage, target_contacts_to_encourage):\n    centers = x.reshape(N, 3)[:, :2]\n    radii = x[2::3]\n    \n    obj_value = -np.sum(radii) # Maximize sum of radii -> minimize negative sum\n\n    # Add penalty for discouraging specific contacts\n    if target_contacts_to_discourage:\n        dist_matrix = squareform(pdist(centers))\n        for i, j in target_contacts_to_discourage:\n            dist_ij = dist_matrix[i, j]\n            r_sum = radii[i] + radii[j]\n            gap = dist_ij - r_sum \n            if gap < EPS_FAR:\n                penalty = BETA_DISCOURAGE * (EPS_FAR - gap) # Penalty increases if circles are too close\n                obj_value += penalty\n    \n    # Add penalty for encouraging specific contacts\n    if target_contacts_to_encourage:\n        dist_matrix = squareform(pdist(centers))\n        for i, j in target_contacts_to_encourage:\n            dist_ij = dist_matrix[i,\
    \ j]\n            r_sum = radii[i] + radii[j]\n            gap = dist_ij - (r_sum + EPS_CLOSE) # If they are further apart than (r_sum + EPS_CLOSE)\n            if gap > 0: # If circles are too far apart (not making contact within tolerance)\n                penalty = ALPHA_ENCOURAGE * (gap)**2\n                obj_value += penalty\n\n    return obj_value\n\ndef _objective_jacobian_nudged(x, target_contacts_to_discourage, target_contacts_to_encourage):\n    grad = np.zeros_like(x)\n    grad[2::3] = -1.0 # Gradient for -np.sum(radii)\n\n    centers = x.reshape(N, 3)[:, :2]\n    radii = x[2::3]\n    dist_matrix = squareform(pdist(centers)) # Precompute distances\n\n    # Jacobian for discouraging contacts\n    if target_contacts_to_discourage:\n        for i, j in target_contacts_to_discourage:\n            dist_ij = dist_matrix[i, j]\n            r_sum = radii[i] + radii[j]\n            gap = dist_ij - r_sum\n            if gap < EPS_FAR:\n                if dist_ij < 1e-10: \n      \
    \              unit_vec_ij = np.zeros(2)\n                else:\n                    unit_vec_ij = (centers[i] - centers[j]) / dist_ij\n                \n                grad[3*i + 0] += -BETA_DISCOURAGE * unit_vec_ij[0]\n                grad[3*i + 1] += -BETA_DISCOURAGE * unit_vec_ij[1]\n                grad[3*j + 0] += BETA_DISCOURAGE * unit_vec_ij[0] # -unit_vec_ij[0] * -BETA\n                grad[3*j + 1] += BETA_DISCOURAGE * unit_vec_ij[1]\n                grad[3*i + 2] += BETA_DISCOURAGE\n                grad[3*j + 2] += BETA_DISCOURAGE\n    \n    # Jacobian for encouraging contacts\n    if target_contacts_to_encourage:\n        for i, j in target_contacts_to_encourage:\n            dist_ij = dist_matrix[i, j]\n            r_sum = radii[i] + radii[j]\n            gap = dist_ij - (r_sum + EPS_CLOSE)\n            if gap > 0:\n                if dist_ij < 1e-10: \n                    unit_vec_ij = np.zeros(2)\n                else:\n                    unit_vec_ij = (centers[i] -\
    \ centers[j]) / dist_ij\n                \n                # Gradient of penalty term ALPHA_ENCOURAGE * (gap)**2\n                # d/dx_c (penalty) = ALPHA_ENCOURAGE * 2 * gap * d/dx_c (gap)\n                # d/dx_c (gap) = d/dx_c (dist_ij - r_sum - EPS_CLOSE) = d/dx_c (dist_ij)\n                # d/dr (gap) = d/dr (-r_sum) = -1.0\n\n                grad[3*i + 0] += ALPHA_ENCOURAGE * 2 * gap * unit_vec_ij[0]\n                grad[3*i + 1] += ALPHA_ENCOURAGE * 2 * gap * unit_vec_ij[1]\n                grad[3*j + 0] += ALPHA_ENCOURAGE * 2 * gap * (-unit_vec_ij[0])\n                grad[3*j + 1] += ALPHA_ENCOURAGE * 2 * gap * (-unit_vec_ij[1])\n                grad[3*i + 2] += ALPHA_ENCOURAGE * 2 * gap * (-1.0)\n                grad[3*j + 2] += ALPHA_ENCOURAGE * 2 * gap * (-1.0)\n    \n    return grad\n\n\ndef _constraints(x):\n    centers = x.reshape(N, 3)[:, :2]\n    radii = x[2::3]\n\n    boundary_constraints = np.empty(4 * N)\n    boundary_constraints[0*N : 1*N] = centers[:, 0] -\
    \ radii  # x - r >= 0\n    boundary_constraints[1*N : 2*N] = 1.0 - (centers[:, 0] + radii) # 1 - x - r >= 0\n    boundary_constraints[2*N : 3*N] = centers[:, 1] - radii  # y - r >= 0\n    boundary_constraints[3*N : 4*N] = 1.0 - (centers[:, 1] + radii) # 1 - y - r >= 0\n\n    dist_matrix = squareform(pdist(centers))\n    overlap_constraints = []\n    for i in range(N):\n        for j in range(i + 1, N):\n            overlap_constraints.append(dist_matrix[i, j] - (radii[i] + radii[j]))\n\n    return np.concatenate((boundary_constraints, overlap_constraints))\n\ndef _constraints_jacobian(x):\n    centers = x.reshape(N, 3)[:, :2]\n    radii = x[2::3]\n    grad = np.zeros((4 * N + N * (N - 1) // 2, N * 3))\n\n    for i in range(N):\n        grad[i, 3*i + 0] = 1.0; grad[i, 3*i + 2] = -1.0\n        grad[N + i, 3*i + 0] = -1.0; grad[N + i, 3*i + 2] = -1.0\n        grad[2*N + i, 3*i + 1] = 1.0; grad[2*N + i, 3*i + 2] = -1.0\n        grad[3*N + i, 3*i + 1] = -1.0; grad[3*N + i, 3*i + 2] = -1.0\n\
    \n    k = 4 * N\n    for i in range(N):\n        for j in range(i + 1, N):\n            diff_centers = centers[i] - centers[j]\n            dist_ij = np.linalg.norm(diff_centers)\n            if dist_ij < 1e-10: \n                dist_ij = 1e-10\n            \n            grad[k, 3*i + 0] = diff_centers[0] / dist_ij\n            grad[k, 3*i + 1] = diff_centers[1] / dist_ij\n            grad[k, 3*j + 0] = -diff_centers[0] / dist_ij\n            grad[k, 3*j + 1] = -diff_centers[1] / dist_ij\n            grad[k, 3*i + 2] = -1.0\n            grad[k, 3*j + 2] = -1.0\n            k += 1\n    return grad\n\n\ndef run_nudging_experiment(base_centers, base_radii, target_contacts_to_discourage=[], target_contacts_to_encourage=[]):\n    \"\"\"\n    Runs a nudging optimization experiment with multi-start local search.\n    \n    Args:\n        base_centers (np.ndarray): N x 2 array of base circle centers.\n        base_radii (np.ndarray): N array of base circle radii.\n        target_contacts_to_discourage\
    \ (list of tuples): List of (i, j) pairs of circles\n                                                      whose contact is to be discouraged.\n        target_contacts_to_encourage (list of tuples): List of (i, j) pairs of circles\n                                                      whose contact is to be encouraged.\n    \n    Returns:\n        tuple: (optimized_centers, optimized_radii, final_score, success_status)\n    \"\"\"\n    best_score = -np.sum(base_radii) # Negative sum for minimization\n    best_centers = base_centers\n    best_radii = base_radii\n    overall_success = False\n\n    for jitter_mag in JITTER_AMPLITUDES:\n        for restart_idx in range(RESTARTS_PER_AMPLITUDE):\n            # Apply perturbation to centers\n            current_centers = base_centers + np.random.uniform(-jitter_mag, jitter_mag, base_centers.shape)\n            current_radii = base_radii \n\n            current_centers = np.clip(current_centers, R_MIN_CONSTRAINT, 1.0 - R_MIN_CONSTRAINT)\n  \
    \          current_centers, current_radii = _local_make_feasible(current_centers, current_radii, eps=TOL)\n\n            initial_guess = np.zeros(N * 3)\n            initial_guess[0::3] = current_centers[:, 0]\n            initial_guess[1::3] = current_centers[:, 1]\n            initial_guess[2::3] = current_radii\n\n            lower_bounds = np.zeros(N * 3)\n            upper_bounds = np.ones(N * 3)\n            lower_bounds[2::3] = R_MIN_CONSTRAINT\n            upper_bounds[2::3] = 0.5 # Max possible radius in unit square\n\n            bounds = Bounds(lower_bounds, upper_bounds)\n            ineq_constraints = {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': _constraints, 'jac': _constraints_jacobian}\n\n            result = minimize(\n                _objective_nudged, \n                initial_guess,\n                method='SLSQP',\n                jac=_objective_jacobian_nudged, \n                bounds=bounds,\n                constraints=[ineq_constraints],\n                options={'maxiter': 500,\
    \ 'ftol': 1e-10, 'disp': False},\n                args=(target_contacts_to_discourage, target_contacts_to_encourage) # Pass both lists\n            )\n\n            if result.success and -result.fun > -best_score: \n                best_score = -result.fun\n                best_centers = result.x.reshape(N, 3)[:, :2]\n                best_radii = result.x[2::3]\n                best_centers, best_radii = _local_make_feasible(best_centers, best_radii, eps=TOL)\n                overall_success = True # At least one run was successful and improved\n    \n    return best_centers, best_radii, -best_score, overall_success # Return actual positive score\n\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    This function serves as the entry point for an evaluation.\n    As this script is a library for nudging optimization, it returns a trivial packing.\n    \"\"\"\n    centers = np.array([[0.5, 0.5]] * N)\n    radii = np.array([1e-3] * N) # Small radii\n    return centers, radii\n\n```\n\n\
    \n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
