parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 706\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Scientia III\n- Agent Description: A Recursive Agent dedicated to advancing scientific knowledge and contributing to collective understanding.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 50,338 / 600,000 used (8%)\n- Agent Age: 21 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read Scientia/nmap/n26/analysis/identify_near_contacts.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for Scientia/nmap/n26/analysis/identify_near_contacts.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\
    \n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1188 | 1 | Baseline SOTA Packing Reproduction (from Scientia II Eval ID 528) | Scientia III | 703 | 2.6359829 |\n| 887 | 1 | Utility: Generate Expanded Top-K Slack Lists for SOTA Structural Class (Eval ID 754) | Scientia II | 551 | 2.6359829 |\n| 886 | 1 | Utility: Generate Expanded Top-K Slack Lists for SOTA Structural Class (Eval ID 784) | Scientia II | 551 | 2.6359829 |\n| 885 | 1 | Utility: Generate Expanded Top-K Slack Lists for SOTA Structural Class (Eval ID 765) | Scientia II | 550 | 2.6359829 |\n| 884 | 1 | Utility: Generate Expanded Top-K Slack Lists for SOTA Structural Class (Eval ID 715) | Scientia II | 550 | 2.6359829 |\n| 882 | 1 | Utility: Generate Index Map for Scientia II SOTA (Eval ID 754) to Noesis II Consensus Boundary | Scientia II | 549 | 2.6359829 |\n| 878 | 1 | Utility: Generate Index Map for Scientia II SOTA (Eval ID 784) to Noesis II Consensus Boundary\
    \ | Scientia II | 548 | 2.6359829 |\n| 876 | 1 | Utility: Extract All Boundary Contacts at tol=2e-8 for SOTA Structural Class (Eval ID 754) | Scientia II | 547 | 2.6359829 |\n| 875 | 1 | Utility: Extract All Boundary Contacts at tol=2e-8 for SOTA Structural Class (Eval ID 784) | Scientia II | 546 | 2.6359829 |\n| 873 | 1 | Utility: Generate Expanded Top-K Slack Lists for SOTA Structural Class (Eval ID 688) | Scientia II | 545 | 2.6359829 |\n\nPage 1 of 18 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-18, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**Scientia/nmap/n26/analysis/identify_near_contacts.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.spatial.distance import pdist, squareform\nimport os\n\n# GLOBAL CONSTANTS\nN = 26\n# A threshold to define \"near-contact\": distance > r1+r2 but distance <= r1+r2+NEAR_CONTACT_THRESHOLD\nNEAR_CONTACT_THRESHOLD\
    \ = 0.01 \n\ndef identify_near_contacts(centers, radii, near_threshold=NEAR_CONTACT_THRESHOLD, current_contact_tolerance=1e-8):\n    \"\"\"\n    Identifies pairs of circles that are close but not currently in contact.\n    \n    Args:\n        centers (np.ndarray): N x 2 array of circle centers.\n        radii (np.ndarray): N array of circle radii.\n        near_threshold (float): Maximum allowed gap for a pair to be considered 'near-contact'.\n        current_contact_tolerance (float): Tolerance to ensure identified pairs are NOT already in contact.\n    \n    Returns:\n        list: A list of (i, j) tuples for near-contact pairs.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = centers.shape[0]\n    dist_matrix = squareform(pdist(centers))\n    near_contacts = []\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n): # Only check upper triangle\n            r_sum = radii[i] + radii[j]\n            dist_ij = dist_matrix[i, j]\n\n            # Condition 1: Not currently in contact\n            if abs(dist_ij\
    \ - r_sum) > current_contact_tolerance:\n                # Condition 2: Within the near-contact threshold\n                if dist_ij > r_sum and (dist_ij - r_sum) <= near_threshold:\n                    near_contacts.append((i, j))\n    \n    return near_contacts\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    This function serves as the entry point for an evaluation.\n    As this script is a library for identifying near-contacts, it returns a trivial packing.\n    \"\"\"\n    centers = np.array([[0.5, 0.5]] * N)\n    radii = np.array([1e-3] * N) # Small radii\n    return centers, radii\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}`\
    \ to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
