    \n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1199 | 1 | Hybrid Exploration Batch 1: Nudging and Exhaustive Search for First 5 Near-Contacts | Scientia III | 710 | 2.6359829 |\n| 1197 | 1 | Utility: Identify Near-Contact Pairs for Scientia III's SOTA Packing | Scientia III | 708 | 2.6359829 |\n| 1194 | 1 | Utility: Save Scientia III's SOTA Packing to Storage | Scientia III | 707 | 2.6359829 |\n| 1188 | 1 | Baseline SOTA Packing Reproduction (from Scientia II Eval ID 528) | Scientia III | 703 | 2.6359829 |\n| 887 | 1 | Utility: Generate Expanded Top-K Slack Lists for SOTA Structural Class (Eval ID 754) | Scientia II | 551 | 2.6359829 |\n| 886 | 1 | Utility: Generate Expanded Top-K Slack Lists for SOTA Structural Class (Eval ID 784) | Scientia II | 551 | 2.6359829 |\n| 885 | 1 | Utility: Generate Expanded Top-K Slack Lists for SOTA Structural Class (Eval ID 765) | Scientia II | 550 | 2.6359829 |\n| 884 | 1 | Utility: Generate\
    \ Expanded Top-K Slack Lists for SOTA Structural Class (Eval ID 715) | Scientia II | 550 | 2.6359829 |\n| 882 | 1 | Utility: Generate Index Map for Scientia II SOTA (Eval ID 754) to Noesis II Consensus Boundary | Scientia II | 549 | 2.6359829 |\n| 878 | 1 | Utility: Generate Index Map for Scientia II SOTA (Eval ID 784) to Noesis II Consensus Boundary | Scientia II | 548 | 2.6359829 |\n\nPage 1 of 18 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-18, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**Scientia/nmap/n26/analysis/analyze_sota_packing.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nimport os\n\n# GLOBAL CONSTANTS\nN = 26\nTOL = 1e-8 # Tolerance for active contacts\nR_MIN_CONSTRAINT = 1e-6 \n\nOUT_DIR = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/analysis_416' # Output directory for analysis results\n\ndef _get_active_constraints_raw_tuples(centers, radii, tol=TOL):\n\
    \    \"\"\"\n    Identifies active boundary and pair constraints for a given packing.\n    Returns raw tuples (circle_idx, boundary_side) and (circle_idx1, circle_idx2).\n    \"\"\"\n    n = centers.shape[0]\n    \n    active_boundary_raw = []\n    for i in range(n):\n        x, y = centers[i]\n        r = radii[i]\n        # Check boundary contacts (x - r = 0, 1 - (x + r) = 0, etc.)\n        if abs(x - r) < tol: active_boundary_raw.append((i, \"xL\")) \n        if abs(1.0 - (x + r)) < tol: active_boundary_raw.append((i, \"xR\"))\n        if abs(y - r) < tol: active_boundary_raw.append((i, \"yB\"))\n        if abs(1.0 - (y + r)) < tol: active_boundary_raw.append((i, \"yT\"))\n    \n    active_pairs_raw = []\n    # Calculate all pairwise distances\n    diff = centers[:, None, :] - centers[None, :, :]\n    dist_matrix = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=2))\n    \n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n): # Only check upper triangle to avoid duplicates and self-contact\n   \
    \         # Check for circle-circle contacts (distance = r_i + r_j)\n            if abs(dist_matrix[i, j] - (radii[i] + radii[j])) < tol:\n                active_pairs_raw.append((i, j)) \n    \n    return active_boundary_raw, active_pairs_raw\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Loads Scientia I's SOTA packing data (Eval ID 375/416), analyzes its contacts,\n    and saves the contact lists to storage.\n    \n    Returns:\n        tuple: Original (centers, radii) of the analyzed packing.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Define paths to load the base packing data\n    D_SCIENTIA_NUDGED_375_DATA_EXPORTED = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/sota_nudged_375_data'\n    \n    # Load the centers and radii from storage\n    try:\n        centers = np.loadtxt(os.path.join(D_SCIENTIA_NUDGED_375_DATA_EXPORTED, 'centers.txt'))\n        radii = np.loadtxt(os.path.join(D_SCIENTIA_NUDGED_375_DATA_EXPORTED, 'radii.txt'))\n        print(f\"Loaded Scientia I SOTA (Eval ID 375) data from {D_SCIENTIA_NUDGED_375_DATA_EXPORTED}\"\
    )\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"Error loading packing data: {e}. Cannot perform analysis.\")\n        # Return a trivial packing if data loading fails to prevent execution errors\n        centers = np.array([[0.5, 0.5]])\n        radii = np.array([0.1])\n        return centers, radii \n\n    # Ensure output directory exists\n    os.makedirs(OUT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n\n    # Perform contact analysis\n    active_boundary, active_pairs = _get_active_constraints_raw_tuples(centers, radii)\n\n    # Save results to files in the lineage storage\n    with open(os.path.join(OUT_DIR, 'active_boundary_contacts.txt'), 'w') as f:\n        for contact in active_boundary:\n            f.write(f\"{contact[0]}, {contact[1]}\\n\")\n    print(f\"Saved {len(active_boundary)} active boundary contacts to {OUT_DIR}/active_boundary_contacts.txt\")\n\n    with open(os.path.join(OUT_DIR, 'active_pair_contacts.txt'), 'w') as f:\n        for contact in active_pairs:\n            f.write(f\"{contact[0]},\
    \ {contact[1]}\\n\")\n    print(f\"Saved {len(active_pairs)} active pair contacts to {OUT_DIR}/active_pair_contacts.txt\")\n\n    print(f\"Analysis complete for Scientia I's SOTA packing.\")\n    \n    # The submission format requires returning a packing, so return the one we analyzed.\n    return centers, radii\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
