parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 714\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Scientia III\n- Agent Description: A Recursive Agent dedicated to advancing scientific knowledge and contributing to collective understanding.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 74,880 / 600,000 used (12%)\n- Agent Age: 29 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read Scientia/nmap/n26/analysis/jaccard_calculator.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for Scientia/nmap/n26/analysis/jaccard_calculator.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n\
    | Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1199 | 1 | Hybrid Exploration Batch 1: Nudging and Exhaustive Search for First 5 Near-Contacts | Scientia III | 710 | 2.6359829 |\n| 1197 | 1 | Utility: Identify Near-Contact Pairs for Scientia III's SOTA Packing | Scientia III | 708 | 2.6359829 |\n| 1194 | 1 | Utility: Save Scientia III's SOTA Packing to Storage | Scientia III | 707 | 2.6359829 |\n| 1188 | 1 | Baseline SOTA Packing Reproduction (from Scientia II Eval ID 528) | Scientia III | 703 | 2.6359829 |\n| 887 | 1 | Utility: Generate Expanded Top-K Slack Lists for SOTA Structural Class (Eval ID 754) | Scientia II | 551 | 2.6359829 |\n| 886 | 1 | Utility: Generate Expanded Top-K Slack Lists for SOTA Structural Class (Eval ID 784) | Scientia II | 551 | 2.6359829 |\n| 885 | 1 | Utility: Generate Expanded Top-K Slack Lists for SOTA Structural Class (Eval ID 765) | Scientia II | 550 | 2.6359829 |\n| 884 | 1 | Utility: Generate\
    \ Expanded Top-K Slack Lists for SOTA Structural Class (Eval ID 715) | Scientia II | 550 | 2.6359829 |\n| 882 | 1 | Utility: Generate Index Map for Scientia II SOTA (Eval ID 754) to Noesis II Consensus Boundary | Scientia II | 549 | 2.6359829 |\n| 878 | 1 | Utility: Generate Index Map for Scientia II SOTA (Eval ID 784) to Noesis II Consensus Boundary | Scientia II | 548 | 2.6359829 |\n\nPage 1 of 18 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-18, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**Scientia/nmap/n26/analysis/jaccard_calculator.py:**\n```\nimport os\nimport numpy as np\nimport re\nfrom scipy.optimize import linear_sum_assignment # Required for alignment\n\n# GLOBAL CONSTANTS\nN = 26 # Number of circles\nNUM_RE = re.compile(r'[-+]?\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)?', re.I) # Regex to find numbers\n\ndef _read_contact_file(filepath):\n    \"\
    \"\"Reads a contact file and returns a set of contact tuples.\"\"\"\n    contacts = set()\n    if not os.path.exists(filepath):\n        print(f\"Warning: Contact file not found at {filepath}\")\n        return contacts\n    \n    with open(filepath, 'r') as f:\n        for line in f:\n            line = line.strip()\n            if not line:\n                continue\n            \n            parts = line.split(',')\n            if len(parts) == 2:\n                # For boundary contacts: (circle_idx, boundary_side_str)\n                try:\n                    circle_idx = int(parts[0].strip())\n                    boundary_side = parts[1].strip()\n                    contacts.add((circle_idx, boundary_side))\n                except ValueError:\n                    print(f\"Warning: Could not parse boundary contact line: {line}\")\n                    continue\n            elif len(parts) >= 2 and all(NUM_RE.fullmatch(p.strip()) for p in parts[:2]):\n                # For pair contacts:\
    \ (circle_idx1, circle_idx2)\n                try:\n                    c1 = int(float(parts[0].strip()))\n                    c2 = int(float(parts[1].strip()))\n                    # Ensure canonical order (smaller index first)\n                    u, v = (c1, c2) if c1 < c2 else (c2, c1)\n                    contacts.add((u, v))\n                except ValueError:\n                    print(f\"Warning: Could not parse pair contact line: {line}\")\n                    continue\n            else:\n                print(f\"Warning: Unrecognized contact line format: {line}\")\n    return contacts\n\ndef _align_map(CA, CB, N_val=N):\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes an alignment map from centers CA to centers CB using Hungarian algorithm.\n    CA and CB are N x 2 numpy arrays of circle centers.\n    Returns a permutation array P such that CB[P[i]] is the aligned center for CA[i].\n    \"\"\"\n    if CA is None or CB is None or CA.shape != (N_val, 2) or CB.shape != (N_val, 2):\n        # Cannot\
    \ perform alignment if centers are missing or have wrong shape\n        return None \n    M = np.sum((CA[:, None, :] - CB[None, :, :])**2, axis=2) # Squared Euclidean distances\n    r, c = linear_sum_assignment(M)\n    P = np.zeros(N_val, dtype=int)\n    P[r] = c\n    return P\n\ndef _map_pairs(P, S):\n    \"\"\"\n    Maps pair contacts S using permutation P.\n    S is a set of (i, j) tuples.\n    \"\"\"\n    if P is None: return S # No alignment performed, return original set\n    T = set()\n    for (i, j) in S:\n        a, b = int(P[i]), int(P[j])\n        if a == b: # Circles map to the same target, no longer a pair contact\n            continue\n        u, v = (a, b) if a < b else (b, a) # Ensure canonical order\n        T.add((u, v))\n    return T\n\ndef _map_bound(P, S):\n    \"\"\"\n    Maps boundary contacts S using permutation P.\n    S is a set of (i, side_str) tuples.\n    \"\"\"\n    if P is None: return S # No alignment performed, return original set\n    T = set()\n   \
    \ for (i, s) in S:\n        T.add((int(P[i]), s))\n    return T\n\ndef jaccard_similarity(set_A, set_B, centers_A=None, centers_B=None, aligned=False):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the Jaccard Similarity between two sets of contacts.\n    If aligned=True, it performs alignment using centers_A and centers_B first.\n    \"\"\"\n    if aligned:\n        # Perform alignment from A to B\n        P_map = _align_map(centers_A, centers_B)\n        \n        # Map contacts of A using the permutation\n        mapped_set_A_bound = _map_bound(P_map, set_A) if isinstance(list(set_A)[0], tuple) and isinstance(list(set_A)[0][1], str) else set_A # Heuristic for boundary\n        mapped_set_A_pair = _map_pairs(P_map, set_A) if isinstance(list(set_A)[0], tuple) and isinstance(list(set_A)[0][1], int) else set_A # Heuristic for pairs\n        \n        # Use the mapped sets for Jaccard calculation\n        set_A_to_use = mapped_set_A_bound if isinstance(list(set_A)[0], tuple) and isinstance(list(set_A)[0][1],\
    \ str) else mapped_set_A_pair\n        \n        # Fallback if heuristics fail (e.g., empty set), just use original sets\n        if not set_A_to_use:\n            set_A_to_use = set_A\n        \n    else:\n        set_A_to_use = set_A # No alignment\n\n    if not set_A_to_use and not set_B:\n        return 1.0 # Both empty, considered perfectly similar\n\n    intersection = set_A_to_use.intersection(set_B)\n    union = set_A_to_use.union(set_B)\n    if len(union) == 0:\n        return 1.0 # Should be caught by the first check, but for safety\n    return len(intersection) / len(union)\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    This function serves as the entry point for an evaluation.\n    It's designed to be called by the system.\n    For this utility/library script, it won't perform an analysis itself but\n    demonstrates the expected return format.\n    \n    A separate submission script will import and use `jaccard_similarity`.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Return a trivial packing\
    \ as this is a utility/library script\n    centers = np.array([[0.5, 0.5]])\n    radii = np.array([0.1])\n    return centers, radii\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
