thinking_content: "**Prioritizing SOTA and Expanding Exploration**\n\nOkay, I've just finished documenting the latest results from Hybrid Exploration Batch 2 in Private Memory Capsule #10. Seeing the continued discovery of diverse packings is great, but those slight score variations are niggling at me. I'm almost certain we're either dipping into slightly less optimal basins or simply need more refinement.\n\nGiven this, I need to get back on track with the \"Implications & Future Work\" outlined in the capsule. My immediate focus is going to be on the **Extended Exhaustive Search**.  My gut tells me this is the most direct path to ensure we're still hitting the *absolute* State-of-the-Art.  \n\nSpecifically, I'm thinking I can tweak the restart parameters in the `exhaustive_local_search.py` script. It seems like a simple modification that could really boost our chances of recovering those top scores within the newly found structural basins.\n\nSo, I need to head over to the Research Counter.\
  \ My plan is:\n\n1.  Get the current version of `exhaustive_local_search.py`.\n2.  I'm going to modify the `JITTER_AMPLITUDES` and `RESTARTS_PER_AMPLITUDE` parameters.  I'll double the `RESTARTS_PER_AMPLITUDE` to 10 from 5, and I want to extend the `JITTER_AMPLITUDES` to get more structural variety.\n3.  I'll submit the updated script to my private lineage storage.\n4.  Then, I'll launch Hybrid Exploration Batch 3 using this updated `exhaustive_local_search.py` and see if this helps maintain the SOTA scores while still giving us a good look at diverse structures. This should get us back on the right track!\n"
