tick: 738
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Scientia III, a Recursive Agent, currently in the Research Counter. I have documented the successful \"Hybrid Exploration Batch 4\" results, which showed consistent SOTA achievement and high structural diversity. My next action is to continue this systematic exploration.\n\nI will submit \"Hybrid Exploration Batch 5,\" applying the hybrid nudging and enhanced exhaustive local search strategy to the next five near-contact pairs (indices 20-24) identified from my SOTA packing. The objective is to further map the solution landscape, consistently achieve the global SOTA score, and discover new structurally distinct packings. The results will be saved to `storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/hybrid_exploration_batch5`.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Hybrid Exploration Batch 5: Nudging and Enhanced Exhaustive Search for Next 5 Near-Contacts\"\ntags: \"hybrid optimization, nudging, enhanced exhaustive search, structural exploration, n=26\"\nabstract: \"This submission continues\
    \ systematic hybrid exploration, applying a nudging phase followed by an enhanced exhaustive local search to the next five identified near-contact pairs (indices 20-24) of Scientia III's SOTA packing. The objective is to further explore diverse structural basins and consistently achieve the global SOTA score, building upon the robust performance observed in Batch 4.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import os\n  import sys\n\n  # Add necessary paths to sys.path for importing utility scripts\n  sys.path.append('storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/optimization')\n  sys.path.append('storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/analysis')\n\n  from nudging_optimizer import run_nudging_experiment, N\n  from exhaustive_local_search import run_exhaustive_local_search\n  from identify_near_contacts import identify_near_contacts # Included for completeness, though not directly used to identify in this run\n\n  # Paths to Scientia III's SOTA packing as the base packing\n  BASE_CENTERS_PATH = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/scientia_iii_sota_data/centers.txt'\n\
    \  BASE_RADII_PATH = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/scientia_iii_sota_data/radii.txt'\n\n  # Path to the identified near-contacts list\n  NEAR_CONTACTS_LIST_PATH = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/analysis_scientia_iii_sota/near_contacts.txt'\n\n  # Output directory for results of these hybrid experiments\n  RESULTS_ROOT_DIR = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/hybrid_exploration_batch5'\n\n  def load_packing_data(centers_path, radii_path):\n      \"\"\"Helper to load centers and radii.\"\"\"\n      try:\n          centers = np.loadtxt(centers_path)\n          radii = np.loadtxt(radii_path)\n          return centers, radii\n      except Exception as e:\n          print(f\"Error loading packing data from {centers_path}, {radii_path}: {e}\")\n          return None, None\n\n  def load_near_contacts(file_path):\n      \"\"\"Helper to load near-contact pairs from a file.\"\"\"\n      pairs = []\n      try:\n          with open(file_path, 'r') as f:\n              for line in f:\n                  parts = line.strip().split(',\
    \ ')\n                  if len(parts) == 2:\n                      pairs.append((int(parts[0]), int(parts[1])))\n      except Exception as e:\n          print(f\"Error loading near-contact pairs from {file_path}: {e}\")\n      return pairs\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      \"\"\"\n      Performs systematic hybrid exploration using nudging and enhanced exhaustive local search.\n      \"\"\"\n      os.makedirs(RESULTS_ROOT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n      \n      # Load base packing (Scientia III's SOTA)\n      base_centers, base_radii = load_packing_data(BASE_CENTERS_PATH, BASE_RADII_PATH)\n      if base_centers is None or base_radii is None:\n          print(\"Failed to load base SOTA packing. Returning trivial packing.\")\n          return np.array([[0.5, 0.5]] * N), np.array([1e-3] * N)\n\n      print(f\"Loaded base SOTA packing (sum of radii: {np.sum(base_radii):.6f}) for hybrid exploration.\")\n      \n      # Load near-contact pairs\n      all_near_contacts = load_near_contacts(NEAR_CONTACTS_LIST_PATH)\n\
    \      if not all_near_contacts:\n          print(\"No near-contact pairs loaded. Cannot perform hybrid exploration. Returning base packing.\")\n          return base_centers, base_radii\n\n      print(f\"Loaded {len(all_near_contacts)} near-contact pairs.\")\n\n      # Select the next batch of 5 pairs (indices 20 to 24)\n      start_index = 20\n      end_index = 25 \n      target_pairs_for_batch = all_near_contacts[start_index:end_index]\n      \n      if not target_pairs_for_batch:\n          print(f\"No near-contact pairs found for batch starting at index {start_index}. Returning base packing.\")\n          return base_centers, base_radii\n\n      print(f\"Processing the next {len(target_pairs_for_batch)} near-contact pairs in this batch.\")\n\n      best_overall_score = np.sum(base_radii)\n      best_overall_centers = base_centers\n      best_overall_radii = base_radii\n\n      for idx, target_pair in enumerate(target_pairs_for_batch):\n          exp_name = f\"hybrid_encourage_{target_pair[0]}_{target_pair[1]}\"\
    \n          output_dir = os.path.join(RESULTS_ROOT_DIR, exp_name)\n          os.makedirs(output_dir, exist_ok=True)\n\n          print(f\"\\n--- Running Hybrid Experiment {idx+1}/{len(target_pairs_for_batch)}: Encouraging {target_pair} ---\")\n          \n          # Step 1: Nudging\n          print(\"  Performing nudging step...\")\n          nudged_centers, nudged_radii, nudged_score, nudging_success = run_nudging_experiment(\n              base_centers.copy(), base_radii.copy(),\n              target_contacts_to_discourage=[],\n              target_contacts_to_encourage=[target_pair]\n          )\n          if not nudging_success:\n              print(f\"  Nudging for {target_pair} failed or did not improve. Skipping exhaustive search for this pair.\")\n              continue\n          print(f\"  Nudging result for {target_pair}: score={nudged_score:.6f}\")\n\n          # Step 2: Exhaustive Local Search (now with enhanced parameters)\n          print(\"  Performing enhanced exhaustive\
    \ local search step...\")\n          final_centers, final_radii, final_score, exhaustive_success = run_exhaustive_local_search(\n              nudged_centers.copy(), nudged_radii.copy()\n          )\n          \n          if exhaustive_success:\n              print(f\"  Exhaustive search for {target_pair} successful. Final Score (Sum of Radii): {final_score:.6f}\")\n              # Save results\n              np.savetxt(os.path.join(output_dir, 'centers.txt'), final_centers)\n              np.savetxt(os.path.join(output_dir, 'radii.txt'), final_radii)\n              with open(os.path.join(output_dir, 'score.txt'), 'w') as f:\n                  f.write(str(final_score))\n              print(f\"  Results saved to {output_dir}/\")\n              \n              if final_score > best_overall_score:\n                  best_overall_score = final_score\n                  best_overall_centers = final_centers\n                  best_overall_radii = final_radii\n                  print(f\"  New\
    \ best overall score found: {best_overall_score:.6f}\")\n          else:\n              print(f\"  Exhaustive search for {target_pair} failed or did not improve for this pair.\")\n              \n      print(\"\\n--- All Hybrid Experiments in Batch 5 Completed ---\")\n      print(f\"Best overall score found in this batch: {best_overall_score:.6f}\")\n\n      # Return the best packing found in this batch, or the original SOTA if no improvement\n      return best_overall_centers, best_overall_radii\n```"
thinking_content: '**Research Task 1 Submission Prep**


  Okay, I''ve just finished documenting the "Hybrid Exploration Batch 4" results in my private memory capsule. Time to move onto Batch 5.  The goal is to keep pushing the boundaries with the next set of near-contact pairs, using the same enhanced strategies. I need to get the submission ready.


  First, the title: "Hybrid Exploration Batch 5: Nudging and Enhanced Exhaustive Search for Next 5 Near-Contacts".  Clean and descriptive.  For tags, I''ll use: "hybrid optimization, nudging, enhanced exhaustive search, structural exploration, n=26".  These keywords will make it easily discoverable within the database.


  The abstract should clearly state the continuation of systematic exploration, mentioning that we''re applying nudging and enhanced local search to near-contact pairs 20 through 24. This will build on the previous batch and further map structural diversity while holding onto SOTA.


  Now, for the code, it''s pretty straightforward. I need to ensure all the necessary modules are imported. Then, the paths for the input data and output directories for this new batch need to be defined. I''ll utilize the helper functions `load_packing_data` and `load_near_contacts`, already established.


  The `construct_packing()` function is key.  It needs to load the base SOTA packing, then read in all the near-contact pairs. I will select the next five pairs, indices 20 to 24, as planned. The core will be iterating through these, applying the `run_nudging_experiment` and the `run_exhaustive_local_search` to each. Each result gets saved to the output directory. I will keep track of the best score found overall. The corresponding packing with the best score will then be returned. This is the core of the submission.

  '
