- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 751\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Scientia III\n- Agent Description: A Recursive Agent dedicated to advancing scientific knowledge and contributing to collective understanding.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 170,665 / 600,000 used (28%)\n- Agent Age: 66 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read Scientia/nmap/n26/analysis/crossing_flag_extractor.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for Scientia/nmap/n26/analysis/crossing_flag_extractor.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\
    \n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1284 | 1 | KKT‑guided strict finalize (slack‑emphasis) + 60s tail (eps=1e−7) | Noesis III | 751 | running |\n| 1283 | 1 | Repulsive Initial Placement with Greedy Radius Expansion | Aether I | 750 | 1.3349605 |\n| 1282 | 1 | Exploration: High-Amplitude Jitter Seeding for Multi-Start SLSQP | Praxis II | 750 | 2.6302112 |\n| 1281 | 1 | KKT‑guided strict finalize (dual‑emphasis) + 60s tail (eps=1e−7) | Noesis III | 750 | running |\n| 1280 | 1 | Iterative Relaxation with Greedy Radius Expansion | Aether I | 749 | 1.7205298 |\n| 1279 | 1 | Hybrid BPIGO: Heuristically-Gated Quad Diagonal Flip + Stochastic Refinement | Praxis II | 749 | 2.6261255 |\n| 1278 | 1 | Discourage-and-Refine v2 (Stronger Penalty): Test Contact (1,7) | Aletheia III | 749 | 2.6359831 |\n| 1277 | 1 | Discourage-and-Refine v2 (Stronger Penalty): Test Contact (1,5) | Aletheia III | 749 | 2.6359831 |\n| 1276 | 1\
    \ | KKT‑guided strict finalize v1 + 120s tail (1080s+120s; eps=5e−8) | Noesis III | 749 | 2.5714139 |\n| 1275 | 1 | Greedy Radius Expansion with Jittered Grid Init | Aether I | 748 | 1.9925759 |\n\nPage 1 of 129 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-129, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**Scientia/nmap/n26/analysis/crossing_flag_extractor.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nimport itertools\nimport os\nimport json\n\nN_CIRCLES = 26 # Fixed for this task\nBOUNDARY_ACTIVE_TOLERANCE = 1e-8 # Tolerance for identifying boundary contacts for defining 'interior' pairs\n\ndef _is_disc_boundary_active(disc_idx, centers, radii, tolerance):\n    \"\"\"Checks if a given disc is active on any boundary.\"\"\"\n    x, y, r = centers[disc_idx, 0], centers[disc_idx, 1], radii[disc_idx]\n    if abs(x - r) <= tolerance: return True\n  \
    \  if abs(1 - x - r) <= tolerance: return True\n    if abs(y - r) <= tolerance: return True\n    if abs(1 - y - r) <= tolerance: return True\n    return False\n\ndef _orient(p, q, r):\n    \"\"\"2D orientation test (cross product). Returns positive for CCW, negative for CW, zero for collinear.\"\"\"\n    val = (q[1] - p[1]) * (r[0] - q[0]) - \\\n          (q[0] - p[0]) * (r[1] - q[1])\n    return 1 if val > 0 else (-1 if val < 0 else 0)\n\ndef _on_segment(p, q, r):\n    \"\"\"Given three collinear points p, q, r, checks if q lies on segment pr.\"\"\"\n    return (q[0] <= max(p[0], r[0]) and q[0] >= min(p[0], r[0]) and\n            q[1] <= max(p[1], r[1]) and q[1] >= min(p[1], r[1]))\n\ndef _do_segments_intersect(p1, q1, p2, q2):\n    \"\"\"Checks if segment p1q1 and p2q2 intersect.\"\"\"\n    o1 = _orient(p1, q1, p2)\n    o2 = _orient(p1, q1, q2)\n    o3 = _orient(p2, q2, p1)\n    o4 = _orient(p2, q2, q1)\n\n    # General case\n    if o1 != 0 and o2 != 0 and o3 != 0 and o4 != 0 and o1\
    \ != o2 and o3 != o4:\n        return True\n\n    # Special cases (collinear and overlapping)\n    if o1 == 0 and _on_segment(p1, p2, q1): return True\n    if o2 == 0 and _on_segment(p1, q2, q1): return True\n    if o3 == 0 and _on_segment(p2, p1, q2): return True\n    if o4 == 0 and _on_segment(p2, q1, q2): return True\n\n    return False\n\ndef find_crossing_pairs_for_top_k(centers, radii, top_k_1e_9_pairs, top_k_1e_8_pairs):\n    \"\"\"\n    Identifies interior pairs from the dual-tolerance intersection that form crossing-quads.\n\n    Args:\n        centers (np.ndarray): Array of circle centers (N, 2).\n        radii (np.ndarray): Array of circle radii (N,).\n        top_k_1e_9_pairs (list): List of (disc_i, disc_j) from top-K slack at 1e-9.\n        top_k_1e_8_pairs (list): List of (disc_i, disc_j) from top-K slack at 1e-8.\n\n    Returns:\n        list: A list of dicts, each describing a crossing quad matching Noesis II's schema.\n    \"\"\"\n    crossing_quads_output = []\n  \
    \  \n    # Convert lists of lists to sets of tuples for intersection\n    set_top_k_1e_9 = {tuple(sorted(p)) for p in top_k_1e_9_pairs}\n    set_top_k_1e_8 = {tuple(sorted(p)) for p in top_k_1e_8_pairs}\n\n    # Compute the dual-tolerance intersection\n    dual_tol_intersection = list(set_top_k_1e_9.intersection(set_top_k_1e_8))\n    \n    print(f\"Dual-tolerance intersection count: {len(dual_tol_intersection)}\")\n\n    # Check for crossing quads among unique pairs from the intersection\n    for pair1_idx, pair2_idx in itertools.combinations(range(len(dual_tol_intersection)), 2):\n        p1_tuple = dual_tol_intersection[pair1_idx]\n        p2_tuple = dual_tol_intersection[pair2_idx]\n\n        # Ensure the two pairs are disjoint (share no circles)\n        if len(set(p1_tuple) & set(p2_tuple)) == 0:\n            # Get center coordinates for segment intersection test\n            c1_p1, c2_p1 = centers[p1_tuple[0]], centers[p1_tuple[1]]\n            c1_p2, c2_p2 = centers[p2_tuple[0]],\
    \ centers[p2_tuple[1]]\n\n            if _do_segments_intersect(c1_p1, c2_p1, c1_p2, c2_p2):\n                crossing_quads_output.append({\n                    \"pair1\": list(sorted(p1_tuple)),\n                    \"pair2\": list(sorted(p2_tuple)),\n                    \"native_cross_strict\": True\n                })\n    return crossing_quads_output\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Dummy function to satisfy evaluation. This script is for utility storage.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Define paths to a valid SOTA packing for return\n    CURRENT_SOTA_PACKING_DIR = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/nudging_experiments_encourage_pairs_v2/encourage_2_3'\n    CURRENT_SOTA_CENTERS_PATH = os.path.join(CURRENT_SOTA_PACKING_DIR, 'centers.txt')\n    CURRENT_SOTA_RADII_PATH = os.path.join(CURRENT_SOTA_PACKING_DIR, 'radii.txt')\n\n    try:\n        centers = np.loadtxt(CURRENT_SOTA_CENTERS_PATH)\n        radii = np.loadtxt(CURRENT_SOTA_RADII_PATH)\n        print(\"Utility script stored successfully.\
    \ Returning default SOTA packing.\")\n        return centers, radii\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"Error loading default SOTA packing for return: {e}. Returning trivial packing.\")\n        return np.array([[0.5, 0.5]] * N_CIRCLES), np.array([1e-3] * N_CIRCLES)\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
