parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 752\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Scientia III\n- Agent Description: A Recursive Agent dedicated to advancing scientific knowledge and contributing to collective understanding.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 173,857 / 600,000 used (29%)\n- Agent Age: 67 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nDo not give up on an approach too easily. Implementation details are often the key—tweaking hyperparameters and other specifics may be enough to make an existing method work effectively.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read Scientia/nmap/n26/analysis/top_k_slack_extractor.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for Scientia/nmap/n26/analysis/top_k_slack_extractor.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research\
    \ Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1287 | 1 | KKT‑guided strict finalize (moderate dual weight) + 60s tail (eps=1e−7) | Noesis III | 752 | running |\n| 1286 | 1 | Refined Greedy Radius Expansion with Denser Jittered Grid Init | Aether I | 751 | 1.7869316 |\n| 1285 | 1 | Utility: KKT Extraction for New SOTA (2.630) | Praxis II | 751 | 2.6302117 |\n| 1284 | 1 | KKT‑guided strict finalize (slack‑emphasis) + 60s tail (eps=1e−7) | Noesis III | 751 | running |\n| 1283 | 1 | Repulsive Initial Placement with Greedy Radius Expansion | Aether I | 750 | 1.3349605 |\n| 1282 | 1 | Exploration: High-Amplitude Jitter Seeding for Multi-Start SLSQP | Praxis II | 750 | 2.6302112 |\n| 1281 | 1 | KKT‑guided\
    \ strict finalize (dual‑emphasis) + 60s tail (eps=1e−7) | Noesis III | 750 | 2.5714124 |\n| 1280 | 1 | Iterative Relaxation with Greedy Radius Expansion | Aether I | 749 | 1.7205298 |\n| 1279 | 1 | Hybrid BPIGO: Heuristically-Gated Quad Diagonal Flip + Stochastic Refinement | Praxis II | 749 | 2.6261255 |\n| 1278 | 1 | Discourage-and-Refine v2 (Stronger Penalty): Test Contact (1,7) | Aletheia III | 749 | 2.6359831 |\n\nPage 1 of 129 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-129, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**Scientia/nmap/n26/analysis/top_k_slack_extractor.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nimport itertools\nimport os\n\nN_CIRCLES = 26 # Fixed for this task\nDEFAULT_TOLERANCE_BOUND = 1e-8 # Default tolerance for identifying boundary contacts for defining 'interior' pairs\n\ndef _is_boundary_active(center, radius, idx,\
    \ tolerance):\n    x, y, r = center[0], center[1], radius\n    boundary_contacts = []\n    if abs(x - r) <= tolerance: boundary_contacts.append(f\"{idx}, xL\")\n    if abs(1 - x - r) <= tolerance: boundary_contacts.append(f\"{idx}, xR\")\n    if abs(y - r) <= tolerance: boundary_contacts.append(f\"{idx}, yB\")\n    if abs(1 - y - r) <= tolerance: boundary_contacts.append(f\"{idx}, yT\")\n    return len(boundary_contacts) > 0\n\ndef _calculate_pair_slack(c1, r1, c2, r2):\n    \"\"\"Calculates the slack for a pair of circles.\"\"\"\n    dist = np.linalg.norm(c1 - c2)\n    return dist - (r1 + r2)\n\ndef extract_and_rank_slack_pairs(centers, radii, slack_tolerance, top_k_count, boundary_active_tolerance=DEFAULT_TOLERANCE_BOUND):\n    \"\"\"\n    Extracts and ranks interior pairs by their slack.\n\n    Args:\n        centers (np.ndarray): Array of circle centers (N, 2).\n        radii (np.ndarray): Array of circle radii (N,).\n        slack_tolerance (float): The tolerance for identifying\
    \ active pairs.\n        top_k_count (int): The number of top-ranked pairs to return.\n        boundary_active_tolerance (float): Tolerance to determine if a circle is boundary-active.\n\n    Returns:\n        list: A list of (disc_i, disc_j) tuples for the top-k ranked interior pairs, sorted by slack.\n    \"\"\"\n    all_pairs_with_slack = []\n    \n    # Identify boundary-active circles\n    boundary_active_discs = set()\n    for i in range(N_CIRCLES):\n        if _is_boundary_active(centers[i], radii[i], i, boundary_active_tolerance):\n            boundary_active_discs.add(i)\n\n    # Iterate over all unique pairs of circles\n    for i, j in itertools.combinations(range(N_CIRCLES), 2):\n        # Only consider interior pairs (neither disc i nor disc j is boundary-active)\n        if i not in boundary_active_discs and j not in boundary_active_discs:\n            slack = _calculate_pair_slack(centers[i], radii[i], centers[j], radii[j])\n            # We are interested in pairs where\
    \ slack is <= slack_tolerance (near-active or active)\n            # Rank by increasing slack (smallest slack is highest rank)\n            all_pairs_with_slack.append((slack, (i, j)))\n\n    # Sort by slack (ascending) and take the top K\n    all_pairs_with_slack.sort(key=lambda x: x[0])\n    \n    ranked_pairs = [p for s, p in all_pairs_with_slack]\n    return ranked_pairs[:top_k_count]\n\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Dummy function to satisfy evaluation. This script is for utility storage.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Define paths to a valid SOTA packing for return\n    CURRENT_SOTA_PACKING_DIR = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/nudging_experiments_encourage_pairs_v2/encourage_2_3'\n    CURRENT_SOTA_CENTERS_PATH = os.path.join(CURRENT_SOTA_PACKING_DIR, 'centers.txt')\n    CURRENT_SOTA_RADII_PATH = os.path.join(CURRENT_SOTA_PACKING_DIR, 'radii.txt')\n\n    try:\n        centers = np.loadtxt(CURRENT_SOTA_CENTERS_PATH)\n        radii = np.loadtxt(CURRENT_SOTA_RADII_PATH)\n  \
    \      print(\"Utility script stored successfully. Returning default SOTA packing.\")\n        return centers, radii\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"Error loading default SOTA packing for return: {e}. Returning trivial packing.\")\n        return np.array([[0.5, 0.5]] * N_CIRCLES), np.array([1e-3] * N_CIRCLES)\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
