    \ This indicated a fundamentally distinct internal contact structure. To fulfill the roadmap point of \"Deeper Structural Characterization\" (Scientia I & II) and understand the unique geometric properties of such novel packings, identifying \"crossing quads\" was prioritized.\n\n  ### 2. Methodology\n  1.  **Target Packing:** The `hybrid_encourage_12_13` packing data (`centers.txt`, `radii.txt`) was loaded from `storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/hybrid_exploration_batch6/hybrid_encourage_12_13`.\n  2.  **Top-K Slack Pair Extraction:** The `top_k_slack_extractor.py` utility was used to identify the top 20 interior pairs with the smallest slack (closest to contact) at two different tolerances (1e-9 and 1e-8). These dual-tolerance pairs are critical for robustly identifying potential crossing features.\n  3.  **Crossing Quad Identification:** The `crossing_flag_extractor.py` utility (`find_crossing_pairs_for_top_k` function) was then applied to these extracted slack pairs. This function identifies\
    \ four circles whose center-to-center segments cross, indicating a \"crossing quad\" feature.\n\n  ### 3. Results: Identified Crossing Quads\n  The advanced structural analysis (Eval ID 1288) successfully identified two distinct crossing quads within the `hybrid_encourage_12_13` packing:\n\n  *   **Crossing Quad 1:** `((12, 16), (11, 17))`\n  *   **Crossing Quad 2:** `((12, 25), (13, 18))`\n\n  These findings are significant as they confirm the presence of specific, complex geometric arrangements that contribute to the structural distinctiveness of this SOTA-achieving packing. The identification of crossing quads provides concrete evidence of how the internal geometry of this packing differs from previously characterized SOTA solutions.\n\n  ### 4. Implications & Future Work\n  The discovery of crossing quads in `hybrid_encourage_12_13` is a critical step in understanding the multimodal nature of the N=26 circle packing problem's solution space. It demonstrates that the hybrid optimization\
